WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.996
First, a fault I planted, in a circuit designed for 10 ms.

2
00:00:05.696 --> 00:00:09.547
Measured time constant: 21.4 ms. Twice as slow.

3
00:00:10.547 --> 00:00:16.236
The first measurement fits two explanations: a larger R or a larger C.

4
00:00:17.436 --> 00:00:20.239
Repeating the unloaded test cannot separate them.

5
00:00:20.839 --> 00:00:22.776
So Spark asks for a known load.

6
00:00:25.976 --> 00:00:28.724
Both models are locked before the next measurement.

7
00:00:29.824 --> 00:00:31.154
Only one survives.

8
00:00:34.654 --> 00:00:37.121
Then it passes a waveform it never saw.

9
00:00:40.621 --> 00:00:45.744
Capacitance ≈ 2.1× design, assuming R = 10 kΩ.

10
00:00:46.744 --> 00:00:48.559
And it says what it still doesn't know.
